cff-version: 1.2.0
title: rapidMQI
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file,
  and cite the method itself: Borri, Corradi, Castori and De Maria (2015),
  "A method for the analysis and classification of historic masonry",
  Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering 13:2647-2665,
  DOI 10.1007/s10518-015-9731-4.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Giovanni
    family-names: Castellazzi
    email: giovanni.castellazzi@unibo.it
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Civil, Chemical, Environmental and Materials Engineering
      (DICAM), University of Bologna, Italy
repository-code: 'https://github.com/gcastellazzi/rapidMQI'
url: 'https://gcastellazzi.github.io/rapidMQI/app/'
abstract: >-
  The Masonry Quality Index of Borri and De Maria, computed in the browser from
  a photograph of the wall. A photograph is scaled from one known distance and
  the seven parameters of the method are assessed against the criteria of the
  original tables, with the minimum length ratio and the dimensions of the
  blocks measured on the image itself. The index is returned for vertical,
  in-plane and out-of-plane actions, with the category of each and with the
  mechanical properties given by the published correlation curves, compared
  against the reference values of the Italian code table. A parameter that
  cannot be inspected may be left open, in which case the index is reported as
  the interval it is known to lie in rather than as a number the survey has not
  earned.
keywords:
  - masonry quality index
  - historic masonry
  - seismic vulnerability
  - visual inspection
  - rule of the art
  - masonry texture
  - structural engineering education
